Behaviour change after upgrading '%9s' to '{:9}' This pyupgrade change (https://github.com/hugovk/yamllint/commit/25e8e9be0838bff930b3b204360fc24385b6edbf) fails indentation-related unit tests which previously passed: ```diff - output += '%9s %s
' % (token_type, + output += '{:9} {}
'.format(token_type, self.format_stack(context['stack'])) ``` https://travis-ci.org/hugovk/yamllint/jobs/459076859#L860 Small example: ```python Python 3.7.1 (default, Nov 6 2018, 18:45:35) [Clang 10.0.0 (clang-1000.11.45.5)] on darwin Type "help", "copyright", "credits" or "license" for more information. >>> '%9s %s
' % ("abc", "def") ' abc def
' >>> '{:9} {}
'.format("abc", "def") 'abc def
' ``` It would have worked if they were integers: ```python >>> '%9s %s
' % (123, 456) ' 123 456
' >>> '{:9} {}
'.format(123, 456) ' 123 456
' ``` --- Another issue with this example, it'd be nice if the indentation of the second line was adjusted, as this often causes flake8 errors. But I understand if this is out of scope of pyupgrade. For example, instead of this: ```diff - output += '%9s %s
' % (token_type, + output += '{:9} {}
'.format(token_type, self.format_stack(context['stack'])) ``` Do this: ```diff - output += '%9s %s
' % (token_type, - self.format_stack(context['stack'])) + output += '{:9} {}
'.format(token_type, + self.format_stack(context['stack'])) ```

